            <title>[LU-20935] Unaligned fallocate(punch_hole) on encrypted file returns 0 but corrupts data inside and outside the punched range</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20935</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Silent data corruption occurs when fallocate(FALLOC_FL_PUNCH_HOLE|FALLOC_FL_KEEP_SIZE) is used on encrypted files with a non-page-aligned offset or length.  &lt;br/&gt;
Users get no error, but the punched bytes are wrong and bytes outside the requested range are also corrupted. This can affect VM and disk images, databases, fallocate --dig-holes, sparse copy tools, and log compaction.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
